  "question": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c453ca27-25c0-4c96-9301-acedee68d939.png\" style=\"width: 650px; height: 122px;\"/></p><p>The total number of hydrogen atoms in product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is__________.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When bromoethane reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> in the presence of ethyl alcohol gives Ethene. </p><p>Similarly When bromoethane reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> in the aqueous medium gives Ethyl alcohol. This reaction is an example of a nucleophilic substitution reaction.</p><p>The reaction is as follows,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d889565c-7948-4b51-92bc-86b1ce37497c.png\" style=\"width: 700px; height: 118px;\"/></p><p>Total number of hydrogen atom in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> that is Ethene and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> that is  Ethyl alcohol is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
